test_command=bash tests/runner_test.sh
id=runner-01 result=green reason=unit tests "runner-01: every tests/*_test.sh suite runs exactly once under the runner, in sorted filename order, and no helper or non-suite file is discovered" + "runner-01: suite discovery is mechanical (the tests/*_test.sh glob) -- a suite added to or removed from the tests dir needs no runner edit" + "runner-01: sorted filename order is mechanical (byte order), not the ambient locale's collation -- a_test.sh runs before ab_test.sh under any locale"
id=runner-02 result=green reason=unit tests "runner-02: an all-green pass prints one status line per suite naming the file with its pass/fail/skip counts, ends with the aggregate summary line, and exits 0" + "runner-02: the runner exits non-zero exactly when a suite exits non-zero -- failing, crashed (counts tallied from PASS/FAIL/SKIP lines), and zero-failure non-zero-exit suites all marked FAILED"
id=runner-03 result=green reason=unit tests "runner-03: one failing suite is isolated and named with its failing scenario ids, every other suite still runs to completion, and the runner exits non-zero" + "runner-03: the failing scenario ids are extracted from the FAIL lines' name prefixes, both the colon-shaped and the space-shaped test-name forms"
id=runner-04 result=green reason=unit test "runner-04: the aggregate summary ends with a measured elapsed-seconds value and a full pass completes under the 120s budget (real-tree end-to-end budget is e2e-qa-02's, verifier-owned)" -- the runner's own budget mechanism (measure and print elapsed) is proven against a fixture pass incl. a 2s suite showing through; the end-state real-tree <120s claim is bought by sibling sub-specs' mechanisms (render-once cache harness-03 green now, nested-execution removal 03/04, frozen-history drops 05) and measured by the verifier's e2e-qa-02
id=runner-05 result=green reason=unit tests "runner-05: -h and --help print usage documenting the one-command invocation, what it runs, the summary line, and the exit contract -- without executing any suite" + "runner-05: the tests/run_all.sh header documents the same; the runner is not a suite -- matches no tests/*_test.sh glob and defines no harness helper"
